## Conclusion: based on the numbers...
## 1) small differences in sources sextracted and rejected for 2nd dataset
## 2) small difference in BKG and BKG uncertaintly of 3rd dataset
## 3) small difference in sources rejected for 3rd dataset
#
## Based on this, I would expect the newer version (2.28.0) of sextractor
## produces the more reliable results...
#
## Altrernatively, to include the 2.28.0 sextractor source in the kit and to get it to compile
## the following would be needed:
# 1) reinplace "s@LM_FINITE finite@LM_FINITE isfinite@" "${worksrcpath}/sextractor/src/levmar/compiler.h"
# 2) "autoreconf -fiv" on sextractor directory
# 3) additional configure command line options required:
#  --enable-openblas --with-openblas-libdir=<OpenBLAS library path> --with-openblas-incdir=<OpenBLAS header dir>
#  --with-fftw-libdir=<FFTW library path> --with-fftw-incdir=<FFTW include dir>
#  --with-cfitsio-libdir=<CFITSIO library path> --with-cfitsio-incdir=<CFITSIO include dir>
#
